                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238549029",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199094653229",
                            "num_reviews": 7,
                            "playtime_forever": 274,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 274,
                            "playtime_at_review": 274,
                            "last_played": 1792886972
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I used to play this game on my Kindle back when I was super young. I loved it so much that when I completed the game, I would immediately start it over again and try playing from the beginning to the end in one sitting. I never actually managed to do that, until I found this game on Steam years later. I finally managed to play it all the way through, and I still love it. I think it looks so beautiful, it looks incredibly pretty, and I found it very enjoyable. \n\nThe cutscenes are honestly not that bad. Sure it's not what you would find in a modern day cutscene, but I personally thought that the cutscenes were pretty well done, especially back when I would play it on my Kindle. Even now playing it, I don't think they're that bad of cutscenes in my opinion. Overall, I really like the atmosphere, the puzzles, and what you actually need to do in the game.",
